{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CROSS-REFERENCE — survey finding relevant to this ticket's operator sign-off gate. From the 2026-08-12 deprecation removal-readiness survey, originally written up on childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet (comment 11) — a scratchpad placement the operator has since ruled an anti-pattern. Survey summary now in session log cosey-vinegarish-mouflon (d0d8-9dfe-f2d8-4364), entry 2.\n\nThe survey placed these keys in Tier 3 (NOT YET — approval-gated AND release-gated, deprecated hours before the survey) and flagged one distinction that must not be lost when this ticket is eventually executed:\n\n- reconciler.resolved_statuses (_config_schema.py:465) is LIVE. It is read by the Jira Data Center adapter (adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py:101 -> backend.py:303). It is NOT a removal candidate, and the \"inert\" language in docs/user-guide.md:498 does NOT apply to it.\n- jira.resolved_statuses (_config_schema.py:490) is the inert one; its only consumer (adapters/jira/probe.py) was deleted with the dormant inbound absence-probe port (task f020, commit b95c097fd4, 2026-08-12).\n\nThe survey also confirmed this ticket's gating state at that time: first AC \"operator sign-off for the removal is recorded on this ticket\" was unchecked and the ticket had zero comments; the decision ticket restful-chaseable-macaw (549c-032f-6cb0-4258) records \"DECISION: deprecate (option 1), do NOT remove now\"."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786588780461970001,"uuid":"1af91bbc-5a06-4303-ac6e-50db74b62d09"}